\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Key Architectural Components:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Pipeline Architecture
\series default
: Implements a 5-stage pipeline comprising Instruction Fetch (IF), Instruction
 Decode (ID), Execute (EX), Memory Access (MEM), and Write-Back (WB), allowing
 instruction-level parallelism and efficient execution flow.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Branch Prediction Unit
\series default
: Improves processor performance by guessing the outcome of branch instructions
 to reduce pipeline stalls.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Memory Subsystem
\series default
: Features instruction and data caches (each 8KB, 2-way set associative),
 with write-back eviction and LRU replacement.
 Includes ITLB/DTLB with Sv32 virtual memory support and a memory protection
 unit (PMA/PMP) supporting up to 64 regions.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Control and Status Registers (CSR)
\series default
: Fully compliant with the RISC-V privileged specification, enabling software
 to interact with exception handling, interrupt control, and processor state.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
This processor supports external interrupts to be service as per the RISC-V
 Privileged specification and hardware interrupt handling.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Exception Handling Unit
\series default
: Detects and manages synchronous events (e.g., illegal instructions, page
 faults), redirecting control flow via trap handlers configured through
 the CSR block.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate

\series bold
Debug Support
\series default
: Integrated debug module enables full system observability, including features
 such as single-step execution, halt/resume control, and execution of commands
 through the program buffer or abstract command interface.
\end_layout

