\begin_layout Subsection
Pipeline Control 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The exception unit may signal the pipeline to flush and ensure that no further
 instructions are executed until the exception is handled.
 This is crucial to prevent further exceptions or incorrect state changes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
When a synchronous (e.g., 
\series bold
\emph on
msie
\series default
\emph default
, 
\series bold
\emph on
mtie
\series default
\emph default
, 
\series bold
\emph on
meie
\series default
\emph default
) or asynchronous exception occurs, the 
\series bold
\emph on
trap_en
\series default
\emph default
 signal is asserted, stalling the pipeline to halt instruction flow.
 Relevant CSR registers are updated with exception details, and the 
\emph on
mtvec
\emph default
 register provides the vector table base address, which is loaded into the
 PC to redirect execution to the exception handler.
 Upon encountering the MRET instruction in the decode stage, the PC is restored
 from the saved address, and the core resumes normal execution.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Handling interrupts in hardware offers several key advantages over software-base
d handling, particularly in real-time and embedded systems where timing
 is critical.
 Hardware interrupt handling significantly reduces interrupt latency, which
 is the time between the occurrence of an interrupt and the start of the
 corresponding interrupt service routine (ISR).
 This is crucial in real-time systems, where deterministic and timely responses
 are required.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
With hardware support, interrupts can be detected and serviced almost immediatel
y, without the overhead of polling or extensive context checks in software.
 The figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Exception-Unit-pipeline"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

 shows the integration of exception unit in with the pipeline
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
\begin_inset Float figure
placement H
wide false
sideways false
status open

\begin_layout Plain Layout
\align left
\begin_inset Graphics
	filename /home/rclab/Documents/SYSTEM CONTROL UNIT/RV32G_EXCEPTION_UNIT.pdf
	scale 50

\end_inset


