 These registers are accessible only when the core enters Debug Mode and
 can be used through standard CSR instructions or abstract debug commands.
 Any attempt to access these registers outside Debug Mode, or on a core
 where they are not implemented, results in an illegal instruction exception.
 This ensures compliance with the RISC-V debug architecture and provides
 essential support for system-level debugging.
