\begin_layout Section
Interrupt Subsystem 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This core utilizes a CLINT-based interrupt architecture, where the irq_i[31:0]
 interrupt signals are managed through the 
\emph on
mstatus
\emph default
, 
\emph on
mie
\emph default
, and 
\emph on
mip
\emph default
 CSRs.
 The core designates the upper 16 bits (irq_i[31:16]) of the 
\emph on
mie
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
mip
\emph default
 registers for custom interrupt handling, reflecting an intentional extension
 to the standard RISC-V CLINT model.
 The figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Interrupt-Platform"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

 shows the interrupt platform integrated with the core.
 
\end_layout

