\begin_layout Standard
For any 
\emph on
irq_i[31:0]
\emph default
 interrupt to become active, both the global interrupt enable (MIE) bit
 in mstatus and the corresponding individual enable bit in the mie register
 must be set.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The interrupts needs to be enabled first during the boot configuration.
 If the corresponding bit in 
\emph on
MIE
\emph default
 is 1, then if that interrupt occurs, it will make the 
\emph on
MIP
\emph default
 bit as 1 indicating that interrupt is pending and needs to be serviced.
 External interrupt bit is cleared once it is serviced, but software and
 timer bits needs to be cleared by writing zero in 
\emph on
MSIP
\emph default
 or 
\emph on
MTIMECMP
\emph default
 register.
