\begin_layout Standard
In the Sv32 virtual memory system, each Page Table Entry (PTE) follows the
 format shown in Figure 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
LatexCommand ref
reference "fig:Sv32-page-table"
plural "false"
caps "false"
noprefix "false"

\end_inset

 .
 The V bit (Valid) determines whether the PTE is considered active—if this
 bit is 0, the rest of the bits in the PTE are ignored by the hardware and
 can be repurposed by software.
 The R, W, and X bits represent access permissions, indicating whether the
 page is readable, writable, and executable, respectively.
 If all three permission bits are cleared (0), the PTE is treated as a pointer
 to a lower-level page table rather than a direct mapping to a physical
 page, identifying it as a non-leaf entry.
 Conversely, if any of the R, W, or X bits are set, the PTE is classified
 as a leaf entry and directly maps a virtual page to a physical page.
 The encoding of RWX bits is shown in figure 
