\begin_layout Standard
The RISC-V debugger architecture is designed to offer precise control and
 inspection capabilities over the processor core while maintaining modularity,
 extensibility, and adherence to the RISC-V Debug Specification (v1.0 Stable).
 The implemented design incorporates a minimal but complete debugging system,
 supporting critical features such as halting and resuming execution, register
 and memory access, single-step operation, and core status monitoring.
 Additionally, several custom debug features have been integrated to enable
 standalone testing of 
\emph on
DM
\emph default
 without being dependent on a working processor core.
\end_layout

