\begin_layout Subsubsection
Custom Debug Registers
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To enable self-validation, system observability, and finer control, several
 custom debug registers have been implemented:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
custom0 (ptr_regno_data):
\series default
 
\emph default
Contains a debug-controlled override value for 
\emph on
regno_data
\emph default
, used during testing when bypassing the RISC-V core.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
custom1 (ptr_data1_data): 
\series default
\emph default
Debug-controlled override for 
\emph on
data1_data
\emph default
 input to the DM.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
custom2 (control mux signal override):
\emph default
 
\series default
Encapsulates all 
\emph on
multi-bit signals
\emph default
 going from the core to the DM, including
\emph on
 CSR write enables
\emph default
, 
\emph on
GPR access signals
\emph default
, and more.
 Used to simulate internal events without actual core activity.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
\emph on
custom3 (lock register):
\emph default
 
