\begin_layout Standard

\series bold
Design Notes:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Single-Hart Simplification:
\series default
 In this single-core design, the 
\emph on
any*
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
all*
\emph default
 fields naturally mirror each other.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Reset Tracking:
\series default
 The 
\emph on
anyhavereset
\emph default
 and 
\emph on
allhavereset
\emph default
 fields help verify whether a reset has occurred after 
\emph on
dmactive
\emph default
 was last set, which is crucial for debugging post-reset behavior.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
No Authentication: 
\series default
Since this implementation operates in a trusted and controlled environment,
 no authentication mechanism is required.
 Accordingly, 
\emph on
authbusy
\emph default
 is hardwired to 0, and 
\emph on
authenticated
\emph default
 is hardwired to 1.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
impebreak Support: 
\series default
This implementation does not support halting the core via the 
\emph on
ebreak
\emph default
 instruction in debug mode.
 Consequently, the 
\emph on
impebreak
\emph default
 field is hardwired to 0.
 Debug entry is achieved through external control via the debug module (e.g.,
 
\emph on
haltreq
\emph default
) rather than software breakpoints.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\emph on
dmstatus
\emph default
 register serves as a vital tool for observing and coordinating the debug
 flow and ensures that the external debugger can operate in a synchronized
 and state-aware manner.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection

\series bold
hartinfo (Address: 0x12):
\series default
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The 
\emph on
hartinfo
\emph default
 register provides static information about a given hart's debug capabilities
 and configuration.
 In a multi-hart system, this register would offer per-hart debug support
 characteristics; however, in this single-hart implementation, it conveys
 basic information applicable to the lone core, as detailed in table 
\begin_inset CommandInset ref
