\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Data Registers:
\series default
 Only two data registers (
\emph on
data0
\emph default
, 
\emph on
data1
\emph default
) are implemented, and they are exclusively used within abstract commands
 for operand and result exchange.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
No dscratch: 
\series default
The optional scratch registers (
\emph on
dscratch0
\emph default
, 
\emph on
dscratch1
\emph default
) are not implemented, as all transient data handling during debug is managed
 internally or via custom registers.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize

\series bold
Non-Memory-Mapped Data Access:
\series default
 The data registers are not memory-mapped for external visibility and are
 instead accessed exclusively through debug commands (e.g., access register,
 access memory).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
This lean configuration simplifies the debug module design while remaining
 compliant with essential portions of the RISC-V Debug Specification.
\end_layout

